IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P9-gate`
IMPORT `P9-art-88-94`

-- Tests for Articles 88 to 94. Expected values are written from the text of the Articles and Article 113 (group General from
-- 2 August 2026; the Articles are not changed by the Omnibus, so 1 August 2026 and 2 August 2026 are the dates that matter,
-- and each function is tested on both sides of that date), never copied from the encoding's own output.

§ `Article 88`

-- args: date asked, the body is the Commission, the matter is the supervision or enforcement of Chapter V
#ASSERT `Art 88(1) the body has the power to supervise and enforce Chapter V` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 88(1) the body has the power to supervise and enforce Chapter V` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Exclusive: another body does not have it.
#ASSERT `Art 88(1) the body has the power to supervise and enforce Chapter V` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Another matter: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT `Art 88(1) the body has the power to supervise and enforce Chapter V` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 88(1) the Commission must entrust the implementation of these tasks to the AI Office` (Date 1 8 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 88(1) the Commission must entrust the implementation of these tasks to the AI Office` (Date 2 8 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 88(1) the duty of the Commission to entrust the implementation of these tasks to the AI Office` (Date 2 8 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 88 the Commission` DOES `Art 88(1) entrust the implementation of the tasks of supervising and enforcing Chapter V to the AI Office` AT 5
-- args: date asked, the exercise of the powers is necessary and proportionate to assist the market surveillance authority
#ASSERT `Art 88(2) the market surveillance authority may request the Commission to exercise the powers laid down in this Section` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 88(2) the market surveillance authority may request the Commission to exercise the powers laid down in this Section` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 88(2) the market surveillance authority may request the Commission to exercise the powers laid down in this Section` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Article 89`

-- args: date asked, the monitoring concerns a provider of a general-purpose AI model, the actions are for the tasks assigned under this Section
#ASSERT `Art 89(1) the AI Office may take the necessary actions to monitor the effective implementation and compliance` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 89(1) the AI Office may take the necessary actions to monitor the effective implementation and compliance` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 89(1) the AI Office may take the necessary actions to monitor the effective implementation and compliance` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 89(1) the AI Office may take the necessary actions to monitor the effective implementation and compliance` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, the person is a downstream provider, the complaint alleges an infringement of this Regulation
#ASSERT `Art 89(2) the downstream provider has the right to lodge a complaint alleging an infringement of this Regulation` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 89(2) the downstream provider has the right to lodge a complaint alleging an infringement of this Regulation` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 89(2) the downstream provider has the right to lodge a complaint alleging an infringement of this Regulation` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 89(2) the downstream provider has the right to lodge a complaint alleging an infringement of this Regulation` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, duly reasoned, indicates (a) the point of contact, indicates (b) the facts, provisions and reason, the downstream provider considers other information relevant, the complaint indicates it
#ASSERT `Art 89(2) the complaint is duly reasoned and indicates at least the required points` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 89(2) the complaint is duly reasoned and indicates at least the required points` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Point (c) is required only where the downstream provider considers other information relevant.
#ASSERT `Art 89(2) the complaint is duly reasoned and indicates at least the required points` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 89(2) the complaint is duly reasoned and indicates at least the required points` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Each of the other points missing, in turn.
#ASSERT `Art 89(2) the complaint is duly reasoned and indicates at least the required points` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 89(2) the complaint is duly reasoned and indicates at least the required points` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 89(2) the complaint is duly reasoned and indicates at least the required points` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Article 90`

-- args: date asked, reason to suspect (a) concrete identifiable risk at Union level, reason to suspect (b) the conditions of Article 51 are met
#ASSERT `Art 90(1) the scientific panel may provide a qualified alert to the AI Office` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 90(1) the scientific panel may provide a qualified alert to the AI Office` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 90(1) the scientific panel may provide a qualified alert to the AI Office` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 90(1) the scientific panel may provide a qualified alert to the AI Office` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 90(1) the scientific panel may provide a qualified alert to the AI Office` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- args: date asked, a qualified alert has been provided, the Commission has informed the Board
#ASSERT `Art 90(2) the Commission may exercise the powers laid down in this Section for the purpose of assessing the matter` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 90(2) the Commission may exercise the powers laid down in this Section for the purpose of assessing the matter` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 90(2) the Commission may exercise the powers laid down in this Section for the purpose of assessing the matter` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 90(2) the Commission may exercise the powers laid down in this Section for the purpose of assessing the matter` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- args: date asked, the AI Office has taken a measure according to Articles 91 to 94
#ASSERT `Art 90(2) the AI Office must inform the Board of any measure according to Articles 91 to 94` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 90(2) the AI Office must inform the Board of any measure according to Articles 91 to 94` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 90(2) the AI Office must inform the Board of any measure according to Articles 91 to 94` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 90(2) the duty of the AI Office to inform the Board of any measure` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 90 the AI Office` DOES `Art 90(2) inform the Board of any measure according to Articles 91 to 94` AT 5
-- args: date asked, duly reasoned, indicates (a) the point of contact, indicates (b) the facts and reasons, the panel considers other information relevant, the alert indicates it
#ASSERT `Art 90(3) the qualified alert is duly reasoned and indicates at least the required points` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 90(3) the qualified alert is duly reasoned and indicates at least the required points` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 90(3) the qualified alert is duly reasoned and indicates at least the required points` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 90(3) the qualified alert is duly reasoned and indicates at least the required points` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 90(3) the qualified alert is duly reasoned and indicates at least the required points` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 90(3) the qualified alert is duly reasoned and indicates at least the required points` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 90(3) the qualified alert is duly reasoned and indicates at least the required points` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Article 91`

-- args: date asked, the request is for documentation under Articles 53 and 55, the request is for additional information necessary to assess compliance
#ASSERT `Art 91(1) the Commission may request the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned to provide the documentation or information` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 91(1) the Commission may request the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned to provide the documentation or information` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 91(1) the Commission may request the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned to provide the documentation or information` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 91(1) the Commission may request the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned to provide the documentation or information` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, the AI Office is about to send a request for information
#ASSERT `Art 91(2) the AI Office may initiate a structured dialogue with the provider before sending the request for information` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 91(2) the AI Office may initiate a structured dialogue with the provider before sending the request for information` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 91(2) the AI Office may initiate a structured dialogue with the provider before sending the request for information` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, the scientific panel has made a duly substantiated request, the access is necessary and proportionate
#ASSERT `Art 91(3) the Commission may issue a request for information to the provider on the request of the scientific panel` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 91(3) the Commission may issue a request for information to the provider on the request of the scientific panel` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 91(3) the Commission may issue a request for information to the provider on the request of the scientific panel` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 91(3) the Commission may issue a request for information to the provider on the request of the scientific panel` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- args: date asked, states the legal basis, states the purpose, specifies what information, sets a period, indicates the fines of Article 101
#ASSERT `Art 91(4) the request for information has the required content` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 91(4) the request for information has the required content` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 91(4) the request for information has the required content` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 91(4) the request for information has the required content` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 91(4) the request for information has the required content` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 91(4) the request for information has the required content` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 91(4) the request for information has the required content` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- args: date asked, the Commission has requested the information
#ASSERT `Art 91(5) the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned must supply the information requested` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 91(5) the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned must supply the information requested` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 91(5) the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned must supply the information requested` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The duty with the period the request sets: 1 September 2026 to 1 October 2026.
-- args: date asked, the Commission has requested the information, the day the period began, the day it ends
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 91(5) the duty of the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned to supply the information requested` (Date 2 9 2026) TRUE (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 1 10 2026) AT (Day (Date 1 9 2026)) WITH
    PARTY `Art 91 the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned` DOES `Art 91(5) supply the information requested` AT (Day (Date 1 10 2026))
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `Art 91(5) the duty of the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned to supply the information requested` (Date 2 9 2026) TRUE (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 1 10 2026) AT (Day (Date 1 9 2026)) WITH
    PARTY `Art 91 the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned` DOES `Art 91(5) supply the information requested` AT (Day (Date 2 10 2026))
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `Art 91(5) the duty of the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned to supply the information requested` (Date 2 9 2026) TRUE (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 1 10 2026) AT (Day (Date 1 9 2026)) WITH
    WAITUNTIL (Day (Date 2 10 2026))
-- No request: nothing is owed. Before the group applies: nothing is owed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 91(5) the duty of the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned to supply the information requested` (Date 2 9 2026) FALSE (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 1 10 2026) AT (Day (Date 1 9 2026)) WITH
    WAITUNTIL (Day (Date 2 10 2026))
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 91(5) the duty of the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned to supply the information requested` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 1 10 2026) AT (Day (Date 1 9 2026)) WITH
    WAITUNTIL (Day (Date 2 10 2026))
-- args: date asked, the Commission has requested the information, the provider is a legal person, a company or a firm, or has no legal personality
#ASSERT `Art 91(5) the persons authorised to represent the provider must supply the information requested on its behalf` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 91(5) the persons authorised to represent the provider must supply the information requested on its behalf` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 91(5) the persons authorised to represent the provider must supply the information requested on its behalf` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 91(5) the persons authorised to represent the provider must supply the information requested on its behalf` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, the lawyer is duly authorised to act for the client
#ASSERT `Art 91(5) a lawyer may supply information on behalf of the client` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 91(5) a lawyer may supply information on behalf of the client` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 91(5) a lawyer may supply information on behalf of the client` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, the information was supplied by a duly authorised lawyer, the information is incomplete, incorrect or misleading
#ASSERT `Art 91(5) the client remains fully responsible` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 91(5) the client remains fully responsible` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 91(5) the client remains fully responsible` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 91(5) the client remains fully responsible` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Article 92`

-- args: date asked, the AI Office has consulted the Board, purpose (a) assess compliance, the information gathered under Article 91 is insufficient, purpose (b) investigate systemic risks
#ASSERT `Art 92(1) the AI Office may conduct an evaluation of the general-purpose AI model concerned` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 92(1) the AI Office may conduct an evaluation of the general-purpose AI model concerned` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Point (a) with the information gathered sufficient: the "where" gate fails.
#ASSERT `Art 92(1) the AI Office may conduct an evaluation of the general-purpose AI model concerned` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Point (b): no gate beyond the consultation.
#ASSERT `Art 92(1) the AI Office may conduct an evaluation of the general-purpose AI model concerned` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Without consulting the Board: the "after consulting" gate fails.
#ASSERT `Art 92(1) the AI Office may conduct an evaluation of the general-purpose AI model concerned` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Neither purpose: the list is not closed, so the text is silent.
#ASSERT `Art 92(1) the AI Office may conduct an evaluation of the general-purpose AI model concerned` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, the appointment is to carry out evaluations on the Commission's behalf
#ASSERT `Art 92(2) the Commission may decide to appoint independent experts to carry out evaluations on its behalf` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 92(2) the Commission may decide to appoint independent experts to carry out evaluations on its behalf` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 92(2) the Commission may decide to appoint independent experts to carry out evaluations on its behalf` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, the expert has been appointed under Article 92(2), the expert meets the criteria of Article 68(2)
#ASSERT `Art 92(2) the independent expert appointed for this task meets the criteria outlined in Article 68(2)` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 92(2) the independent expert appointed for this task meets the criteria outlined in Article 68(2)` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 92(2) the independent expert appointed for this task meets the criteria outlined in Article 68(2)` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 92(2) the independent expert appointed for this task meets the criteria outlined in Article 68(2)` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, the request is for the purposes of an evaluation under Article 92(1), the access is through APIs or further appropriate technical means and tools, including source code
#ASSERT `Art 92(3) the Commission may request access to the general-purpose AI model concerned` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 92(3) the Commission may request access to the general-purpose AI model concerned` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 92(3) the Commission may request access to the general-purpose AI model concerned` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 92(3) the Commission may request access to the general-purpose AI model concerned` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, states the legal basis, states the purpose and reasons, sets the period, states the fines of Article 101
#ASSERT `Art 92(4) the request for access has the required content` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 92(4) the request for access has the required content` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 92(4) the request for access has the required content` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 92(4) the request for access has the required content` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 92(4) the request for access has the required content` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 92(4) the request for access has the required content` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- args: date asked, the Commission has requested the information or access
#ASSERT `Art 92(5) the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned must supply the information requested` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 92(5) the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned must supply the information requested` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 92(5) the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned must supply the information requested` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
